ays near the fundamentals-based estimate of about seven points.", "watch": "A late shift among South Texas Latino voters toward Tijerina, or fresh polling showing a tighter race, would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 46 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Henry Cuellar (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Henry Cuellar, one of the most conservative Democrats in the House, seeks another term in a South Texas district that was redrawn to lean Republican. He faces Tano Tijerina, a Webb County judge who switched parties and has campaigned with national GOP support, plus a Green Party candidate on the ballot.\n\nCuellar has out-raised Tijerina and holds a cash advantage, and prediction markets price his chances near 89 percent. Expert ratings cluster between Tilt D and Likely D. The only recent independent poll, from August, showed Cuellar up 11 points, though polling here is sparse and aging. The race looks like a genuine but manageable incumbent advantage, with Cuellar favored by roughly seven points and meaningful uncertainty about how the redrawn electorate behaves.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9009, "margin": 7.69}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8765, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8779, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8804, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8627, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8617, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8973, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8968, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9013, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9125, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8966, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8974, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8927, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7979, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.838, "margin": 7.0},